  "step_2": "The individual states: 'Ich gehe den sicheren Weg und entscheide mich für eine 100% Wahrscheinlichkeit Geld zu gewinnen, da mir der Unterschied zwichen dem Gewinn von A und B zu gering erscheint.' This translates to: 'I take the safe route and choose the 100% probability of winning money, because the difference between the winnings of A and B seems too small to me.' The individual considers the certainty of outcome (A has 100% chance of winning, B has a 50-50 gamble) and perceives the difference in outcomes as negligible. The justification is based on risk aversion and perceived similarity in the payoff difference, not on skewness. No mention is made of skewness, distribution asymmetry, or the relative probability mass on favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes. Thus, the deliberation process centers on perceived risk and payoff difference, not on skewness.",
